From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:37:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] download: let a running download be stopped

abort_download(msg_id) dequeues an in-progress download and puts the
message back to Available, so the download button returns. It is one
conditional UPDATE (InProgress -> Available): a download finishing in
between sets Done, which must not be turned back.

A queued download's chunk loop checks before every chunk that its
`download` row still exists and yields if it is gone. It checks the row,
not the download state: queued auto-downloads stay Available with their
row present the whole time. Yielding keeps the staging file, so
downloading again resumes at the byte offset until housekeeping reclaims
the file, and never deletes a row the user re-created by tapping again.

A whole-message fetch on a server without partial FETCH cannot be
interrupted and still completes. Exposed over JSON-RPC as abort_download.
---
 deltachat-jsonrpc/src/api.rs |   8 +
 src/download.rs              | 288 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 269 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

